/-!
# J₂ and HS preliminaries for Chapter 16

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, 16.1.5(8),(10),
16.1.6 and their uses in 16.1.7–8, printed pp.1172–1173.

The completed calculations identify the full J₂ automorphism group with the
checked permutation extension, cover every inner involution by the two
representatives, and prove the central representative's A₅/(Q₈ * D₈) shape.
The general exclusion lemma removes components once the actual normal
two-kernel is proved self-centralizing.

The remaining representative structures, kernel actions, component
identifications, Sylow index bounds, and arbitrary two-element innerness
are not asserted here. `Statements` specifies the exact remaining source
alternatives, retaining normality, nonsplit extension notation and actual
model isomorphisms. Final assembly remains in this module.
-/
